// DRed PHASE 3 — RE-DERIVE. THE CLAIM IS THAT `_i` *IS* PHASE 3, AND THIS FILE
// IS WHERE THAT CLAIM IS EXERCISED RATHER THAN ASSERTED.
//
// ── WHAT PHASE 3 IS, MECHANICALLY ─────────────────────────────────────────
// There is NO fourth emitted sibling. Phase 3 is the SAME item `_i` that the
// insert path uses, re-entered with two substitutions:
//
//   __wql_tc_scc0_i( PRES ,  &mut tot )      ← tot EXACTLY AS `_cpt` LEFT IT
//                     ^^^^ the SURVIVOR edb, where an insert epoch passes the
//                          ACCUMULATED edb
//
// and the re-derived rows are the suffix `[b0 .. len)` with
//
//   ⚠ b0 CAPTURED **AFTER** `_cpt` RETURNS.
//
// That capture point is not a detail. On the insert path `__b0_<m>` is taken
// BEFORE the driver call, because nothing shrinks the total there. `_cpt`
// SHRINKS it (retain, then `pop` to the write index), so a `b0` captured before
// the compact indexes a vector that no longer reaches that length: on the chain
// below it would be 6 against a post-compact length of 2. The fixture asserts
// `b0 == |S|` straight from the latch, which is the machine-checkable form of
// "captured on the right side of the compact".
//
// ── `__tot := S`, AND WHY `tot = 0` WOULD HAVE BEEN A BUG ─────────────────
// The plan for this phase said "tot = 0, shadow set pre-populated with S".
// ⚠ IN `_i` THE SHADOW SET AND THE TOTAL ARE THE SAME VARIABLE — the incr state
// block seeds a FRESH `__rs_<m>` by walking `__tot_<m>` element by element. So
// `tot = 0` is an EMPTY shadow set, every surviving fact counts as new, and the
// whole closure is recomputed. The ANSWER IS STILL RIGHT. Only incrementality
// dies — which is why this file asserts `RD`, not the answer.
// ⚠ THAT IS NOT A WARNING IN A COMMENT — IT IS A LIVE BLOCK AT THE BOTTOM OF
// THIS FILE. `_i` is called on the diamond's survivor edb with a FRESH EMPTY
// Vec, and the file ASSERTS BOTH HALVES: the resulting relation equals
// `closure(PRES)` exactly (the answer is RIGHT), and it holds 4 rows where the
// correct `RD` is 1 (the incrementality is GONE). Only the numbers this file
// actually computes are claimed; the chain's and the cycle's are not, because
// they were not run.
//
// ── THE SURVIVOR LEMMA, ASSERTED AS ITS OWN CHECK: `S ⊆ closure(PRES)` ────
// ⚠⚠ THIS IS THE ASSERTION NO OTHER FIXTURE IN THE ARC MAKES, AND IT IS THE ONE
// THAT CANNOT BE RECOVERED LATER. Phase 3 only ever APPENDS (`promote` pushes),
// so ANY row phase 2 wrongly KEEPS is in the answer forever — unrepairable by
// construction. The soundness of phases 1+2 TOGETHER is exactly
// `S = T ∖ OD ⊆ lfp(PRES)`, and `wql_incr_rel_od_phase1.logos` cannot see it:
// that file checks `S` against `T ∖ OD_oracle`, so an engine and an oracle
// sharing a wrong theorem about OD would agree with each other and both be
// wrong. Here `S` is walked ROW BY ROW against `naive_closure(PRES)` — a
// from-scratch fixpoint that knows nothing about OD, DE, or phases.
// It is also the hypothesis `_i`'s completeness proof now names: the insert
// caller discharges `T₀ ⊆ lfp(E')` by monotonicity, and this caller — whose
// input SHRINKS, so monotonicity is FALSE — discharges it by this lemma.
//
// ── WHAT EACH CELL IS FOR ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  1 CHAIN, mid edge deleted   — `RD = ∅`. The boundary: phase 2 alone is
//                                already the right answer, so phase 3 must add
//                                NOTHING. Every "re-derive everything" defect
//                                shows up here as a non-empty RD.
//  2 DIAMOND                   — `RD = {(1,4)}`, and it is re-derived from an
//                                OLD S-row `(1,3)` joined with an OLD PRES edge
//                                `(3,4)`. NEITHER side is a delta, so this row
//                                exists ONLY because `_i`'s round 0 is a FULL
//                                naïve pass. It is the cell that fails the
//                                moment round 0 is narrowed to the base bodies.
//  3 SELF-SUPPORTING CYCLE     — `S = ∅`, `RD` = the whole four-row closure.
//                                Phase 2 answers nothing at all here; phase 3
//                                is the entire answer.
//  4 DE EMPTY                  — `OD = ∅`, `S = T`, `RD = ∅`. A phase 3 that
//                                re-derived on principle rather than on need
//                                shows up here and nowhere else, and a
//                                DUPLICATE-pushing `_i` shows up here as a
//                                relation longer than its own closure.
//
// ── THE ORACLES ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// `naive_closure` is repeat-`P := P ∪ (P ∘ E)` with linear dedup — no delta, no
// shadow set, no SCC, no phases. `RD` is checked against
// `closure(PRES) ∖ S` computed from it, `|RD|` additionally against a
// HAND-COMPUTED count per cell, and `RD ⊆ rm` against the negative delta `_cpt`
// handed back. `stdlib/mem/deem/incr_rec.logos`'s `dred` runs the same algorithm
// as the emitter and is cited nowhere as agreement.
//
// ── CONTROLS, MEASURED 2026-08-08 (archives dropped, whole stdlib rebuilt) ─
//  • ROUND 0 NARROWED TO THE BASE BODIES — `emit_scc_fn`'s seed selection
//    `if incr || oc1.n == 0i64` weakened to `if oc1.n == 0i64`, i.e. the
//    "exact" delta-only round 0 the header names as the follow-up.
//    → **exit 62** — the DIAMOND, at the SET check (50 + 12). `(1,4)` is
//    `S(1,3) ⋈ PRES(3,4)`: both sides are old, so no delta occurrence produces
//    it, `RD` comes back EMPTY and the relation is missing a true fact.
//    Predicted before running. The CHAIN stays green — its RD is empty anyway —
//    so this cell is the only one that speaks, and it speaks at the ANSWER
//    check rather than at the RD check because a missing row breaks both and
//    the set comparison is written first.
//  • THE SHADOW SET NOT SEEDED FROM THE TOTAL — `emit_scc_fn`'s `if incr` state
//    arm forced to the from-scratch arm.
//    → **exit 42** — the CHAIN, at the SET check (30 + 12): S = [12,34] is
//    re-derived and pushed a SECOND time, so the relation comes back with four
//    rows where its closure has two. Predicted as cell 4 and MEASURED at cell 1,
//    which is the earlier cell with the same shape — the prediction named the
//    defect correctly and the cell index wrongly, and is corrected here rather
//    than quietly re-fitted.
//  • THE `b0` CAPTURE MOVED BACK BEFORE `_cpt` (this file's own call sequence,
//    since that capture is the caller's).
//    → **exit 40** — the chain (30 + 10): `b0 = 6` against a post-compact
//    length of 2 and a `|S|` latch of 2. The suffix would have been empty
//    either way, which is exactly why `b0 == |S|` is ASSERTED and not left to
//    be inferred from RD.
//
// ── CONTROLS FOR THE COST GATE, MEASURED 2026-08-08 (archives dropped, whole
// ── stdlib rebuilt for each) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//  • WORK DOUBLED — `member_block_frag` splices its `runs` TWICE, so every body
//    of every member runs twice in every round of `_i`, `_od`, `_odp` and the
//    from-scratch driver. The dedup gate makes that IDEMPOTENT: every answer,
//    every set, every cardinality in this arc is unchanged and the machine does
//    exactly twice the work.
//    → **exit 22** — cell 1's counter, 4 against 2. Predicted before running.
//    ⚠⚠ AND THE TWO SIBLING FIXTURES **PASSED** UNDER IT:
//    `wql_incr_rel_dred_product_random` (random shapes, product-automaton
//    oracle, phases 1+2+3 end to end) and `wql_incr_rel_od_phase1_adv` (eleven
//    graphs, a six-epoch mixed insert/retract run) both stayed GREEN while the
//    engine did double the work. THAT is the measurement that says this counter
//    is not decoration: it is the only thing in the tree that saw it.
//  • THE COUNTER MOVED INSIDE THE ACCEPT ARM — `rel_push_frag`'s increment put
//    into the `if __rsp.insert(…)` branch, i.e. counting rows KEPT instead of
//    rows PRODUCED. This is the "free" counter (`__out.len()`, already
//    recoverable as the suffix past `b0`) that the header argues against.
//    → **exit 22** — cell 1 reads 0. Every one of its 2 candidates was dropped
//    by the dedup gate, so an accept counter reports that the retraction cost
//    NOTHING. Predicted before running. This is the placement control: the
//    number is only a sensor on one side of that `if`.
//  • CELL 5's n=8 LITERAL PERTURBED 28 → 29 (this file's own number, fixture
//    rebuild only) → **exit 172**, so the cost gate's counts are asserted and
//    not decoration — the same control this arc's sibling files run on their
//    hand-computed cardinalities.
//
// ⚠ NO CONTROL IS RECORDED FOR THE *IMPROVEMENT* DIRECTION, and that is a real
// gap rather than an omission: the change that would drop the count below |S| is
// the delta-only round 0, and it is ALREADY MEASURED ABOVE as **exit 62** — it
// breaks the ANSWER at cell 2 before any counter is read. So the claim "this
// cell goes red when the pessimization is fixed" is argued from the arithmetic
// (a round 0 that skips the S ⋈ PRES join cannot produce (n−1)(n−2)/2
// candidates) and is NOT measured, because the only defect that produces it also
// produces a wrong relation. The measurement arrives with the hybrid.
//
// ── WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* HERE ───────────────────────────────────────
// NO RETRACTION SURFACE. `incr_retract_eligible` still refuses every rel-backed
// query; `tc_retract` / `tc_apply` / `__wd` do not exist, and
// `fail/wql_incr_rel_no_retract.logos` and the two `fail/wql_incr_mutrec_no_retract_*`
// doors are UNCHANGED. This file drives the four emitted private siblings
// directly, as a sibling item in the same module — which is why phase 3 can be
// proven before any surface exists.
// NO `|RD|` LATCH. `_cpt` still reports `-1` in slot 2 and this file asserts it,
// because `_cpt` returns BEFORE phase 3 runs and so structurally cannot fill it;
// the epoch driver retires the sentinel, and there is no epoch driver. Writing
// the fill here would assert the fixture's own arithmetic against itself. What
// IS asserted is the quantity that line would carry:
// `tot.len() - lat[1]` against the closure oracle.
//
// ── THE COST GATE — `_i`'s `__wc` OUT-PARAM, ADDED 2026-08-08 ─────────────
// `_i` now reports CANDIDATE ROWS (produced by a body, accepted or dropped),
// one i64 per SCC member — see `rel_push_frag`'s `__wcp` note and the `__wc`
// note on `emit_scc_fn`'s signature for what it counts and why it is not
// `__out.len()`. Every cell pins its exact count; CELL 5 is the gate proper: a
// chain of n edges with the LAST one retracted at n = 8 and n = 16, where the
// count is provably `n(n−1)/2 = |S|` while `RD = ∅`. Work linear in the
// relation, zero rows of output — the PESSIMIZATION recorded in
// `emit_scc_od_fns`'s header, pinned so it cannot deepen or be repaired
// silently. ⚠ It counts ROWS, not scans, and every cell here is N = 1.
//
// exit 0 = on all four cells: `S ⊆ closure(PRES)` row by row; `b0 == |S|`; the
// post-phase-3 relation equals the from-scratch fixpoint over PRES as a SET and
// its first `|S|` rows are still exactly `S`; `RD` equals `closure(PRES) ∖ S`
// as a set and matches a hand-computed count; `RD ⊆ rm`; and the `-1` sentinel
// is untouched.
package test;

use logos.std.wql.wql;
use logos.std.wql.el;
use logos.lang.result;
use logos.mem.collections.vec;

struct E { pub a: i64, pub b: i64 }

pub deem tc(es: &[E]) {
    rel path(a: i64, b: i64) {
        from es e select (e.a, e.b);
        from path p join es e on p.b == e.a select (p.a, e.b);
    }
    from path p group by p.a aggregate c = count() select (key, c)
}

// ── THE ORACLE: a from-scratch naive closure. `P := E ∪ (P ∘ E)` to
// quiescence, dedup by linear `==`. No delta, no shadow set, no phases.
fn pair_uniq(p: &mut Vec<(i64, i64)>, a: i64, b: i64) -> bool {
    let mut i: i64 = 0i64;
    while i < p.len() {
        let c: (i64, i64) = p.get(i);
        if c.0 == a && c.1 == b { return false; }
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
    p.push((a, b));
    return true;
}

fn pair_has(p: &Vec<(i64, i64)>, a: i64, b: i64) -> bool {
    let mut i: i64 = 0i64;
    while i < p.len() {
        let c: (i64, i64) = p.get(i);
        if c.0 == a && c.1 == b { return true; }
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
    return false;
}

fn naive_closure(es: &[E]) -> Vec<(i64, i64)> {
    let mut p: Vec<(i64, i64)> = vec_new::<(i64, i64)>();
    let mut i: i64 = 0i64;
    while i < es.len() {
        pair_uniq(&mut p, es[i].a, es[i].b);
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
    let mut grew: bool = true;
    while grew {
        grew = false;
        let mut k: i64 = 0i64;
        while k < p.len() {
            let pr: (i64, i64) = p.get(k);
            let mut j: i64 = 0i64;
            while j < es.len() {
                if pr.1 == es[j].a {
                    if pair_uniq(&mut p, pr.0, es[j].b) { grew = true; }
                }
                j = j + 1i64;
            }
            k = k + 1i64;
        }
    }
    return p;
}

// Set equality: mutual containment PLUS equal length, so a DUPLICATE in either
// side is a disagreement rather than something containment absorbs. That is the
// only thing standing between this file and an `_i` whose shadow set stopped
// gating.
fn same_set(x: &Vec<(i64, i64)>, y: &Vec<(i64, i64)>) -> bool {
    if x.len() != y.len() { return false; }
    let mut i: i64 = 0i64;
    while i < x.len() {
        let c: (i64, i64) = x.get(i);
        if !pair_has(y, c.0, c.1) { return false; }
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
    let mut j: i64 = 0i64;
    while j < y.len() {
        let c2: (i64, i64) = y.get(j);
        if !pair_has(x, c2.0, c2.1) { return false; }
        j = j + 1i64;
    }
    return true;
}

fn seq_eq(x: &Vec<(i64, i64)>, y: &Vec<(i64, i64)>) -> bool {
    if x.len() != y.len() { return false; }
    let mut i: i64 = 0i64;
    while i < x.len() {
        let a: (i64, i64) = x.get(i);
        let b: (i64, i64) = y.get(i);
        if a.0 != b.0 || a.1 != b.1 { return false; }
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
    return true;
}

fn pair_copy(x: &Vec<(i64, i64)>) -> Vec<(i64, i64)> {
    let mut o: Vec<(i64, i64)> = vec_new::<(i64, i64)>();
    let mut i: i64 = 0i64;
    while i < x.len() { let c: (i64, i64) = x.get(i); o.push((c.0, c.1)); i = i + 1i64; }
    return o;
}

fn ed(a: i64, b: i64) -> E { return E { a: a, b: b }; }

fn edge_has(v: &Vec<E>, a: i64, b: i64) -> bool {
    let mut i: i64 = 0i64;
    while i < v.len() {
        let e: E = v.get(i);
        if e.a == a && e.b == b { return true; }
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
    return false;
}

fn survivors(all: &Vec<E>, de: &Vec<E>) -> Vec<E> {
    let mut out: Vec<E> = vec_new::<E>();
    let mut i: i64 = 0i64;
    while i < all.len() {
        let e: E = all.get(i);
        if !edge_has(de, e.a, e.b) { out.push(e); }
        i = i + 1i64;
    }
    return out;
}

// ── ONE CELL: THE WHOLE FOUR-PHASE SEQUENCE ────────────────────────────────
// T ← from-scratch; OD ← 1a+1b; (S, rm) ← 2; RD ← 3.
//
// ⚠ HOW MUCH WORK THE BROKEN CODE DOES BEFORE ANYTHING IS LOOKED AT: the
// from-scratch fixpoint over ALL, then phase 1a's scan of the whole previous
// total against DE, then 1b to quiescence over the survivor graph, then `_cpt`'s
// counting pass over all of T and its retain pass over all of T, then `_i`'s
// round-0 naïve pass over (S × PRES) and its delta rounds to quiescence. Nothing
// here is caught at a first push.
fn cell_p3(all: &Vec<E>, de: &Vec<E>, want_s_n: i64, want_rd_n: i64,
           wc_out: &mut Vec<i64>) -> i32 {
    let pres: Vec<E> = survivors(all, de);
    let cl_pres: Vec<(i64, i64)> = naive_closure(pres.as_slice());

    // ── T, from the emitter's own from-scratch driver ────────────────────
    let mut tot: Vec<(i64, i64)> = vec_new::<(i64, i64)>();
    match __wql_tc_scc0(all.as_slice(), &mut tot) {
        Result::Ok(_u) => { } Result::Err(_e) => { return 1i32; }
    }
    let cl_all: Vec<(i64, i64)> = naive_closure(all.as_slice());
    if !same_set(&tot, &cl_all) { return 2i32; }

    // ── PHASE 1a + 1b ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    let mut od: Vec<(i64, i64)> = vec_new::<(i64, i64)>();
    match __wql_tc_scc0_od(de.as_slice(), tot.as_slice(), &mut od) {
        Result::Ok(_u) => { } Result::Err(_e) => { return 3i32; }
    }
    match __wql_tc_scc0_odp(pres.as_slice(), &mut od) {
        Result::Ok(_u) => { } Result::Err(_e) => { return 4i32; }
    }

    // ── PHASE 2 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    let mut lat: Vec<i64> = vec_new::<i64>();
    let mut rm: Vec<(i64, i64)> = vec_new::<(i64, i64)>();
    match __wql_tc_scc0_cpt(od.as_slice(), &mut tot, &mut rm, &mut lat) {
        Result::Ok(_u) => { } Result::Err(_e) => { return 5i32; }
    }
    if lat.len() != 3i64 { return 6i32; }
    if lat.get(1i64) != tot.len() { return 7i32; }        // |S|
    if tot.len() != want_s_n      { return 8i32; }        // hand-computed

    // ⚠⚠ THE SURVIVOR LEMMA, ROW BY ROW: `S ⊆ closure(PRES)`.
    // This is the soundness of phases 1 AND 2 TOGETHER, and the ONE property
    // phase 3 cannot repair — it only appends, so a row wrongly kept here is
    // wrong forever. The oracle is a from-scratch closure over the survivor
    // edges that has never heard of OD, DE or a phase.
    let mut sl: i64 = 0i64;
    while sl < tot.len() {
        let sc: (i64, i64) = tot.get(sl);
        if !pair_has(&cl_pres, sc.0, sc.1) { return 9i32; }
        sl = sl + 1i64;
    }

    // The exact rows of S, kept so that "phase 3 only APPENDS" is checkable
    // afterwards rather than assumed from the emitter's `promote`.
    let s_snap: Vec<(i64, i64)> = pair_copy(&tot);

    // ⚠ THE CAPTURE POINT. `b0` is taken HERE — after `_cpt` shrank the total —
    // and not before the phase-2 call the way the insert driver takes it. The
    // latch `|S|` is the independent witness that it landed on the right side.
    let b0: i64 = tot.len();
    if b0 != lat.get(1i64) { return 10i32; }

    // ── PHASE 3 — `_i`, OVER THE SURVIVOR EDB, ON THE COMPACTED TOTAL ────
    // `__tot := S`, passed by handing `_cpt`'s own `&mut` Vec straight on. The
    // shadow set is therefore S (it is seeded by walking this Vec), so the
    // round-0 naïve pass re-derives freely and the dedup gate drops everything
    // already present: what lands in the suffix is exactly what was missing.
    match __wql_tc_scc0_i(pres.as_slice(), &mut tot, wc_out) {
        Result::Ok(_u) => { } Result::Err(_e) => { return 11i32; }
    }
    // ⚠ THE COST GATE'S RAW READING lands in `wc_out` and is asserted in
    // `main`, NOT here. This fn's exit codes 1..19 are packed and its callers
    // offset them by 20 (30/50/70/90 — see the recorded controls at the head of
    // this file, exits 62 / 42 / 40), so a 20th code here would alias the next
    // cell's base. The counter's checks therefore live one frame up, where the
    // codes are free and where each cell's expected number can be written
    // beside the shape it follows from.

    // THE FIXPOINT. The maintained relation now equals the from-scratch fixpoint
    // over `I ∖ R`, as a SET — length included, so a re-derivation that pushed a
    // duplicate is a failure and not a rounding.
    if !same_set(&tot, &cl_pres) { return 12i32; }

    // PHASE 3 ONLY APPENDS: the first `|S|` rows are still exactly S, in order.
    let mut pre: Vec<(i64, i64)> = vec_new::<(i64, i64)>();
    let mut pi: i64 = 0i64;
    while pi < b0 { let pc: (i64, i64) = tot.get(pi); pre.push((pc.0, pc.1)); pi = pi + 1i64; }
    if !seq_eq(&pre, &s_snap) { return 13i32; }

    // ── RD, THE RE-DERIVED SUFFIX `[b0 .. len)` ──────────────────────────
    let mut rd: Vec<(i64, i64)> = vec_new::<(i64, i64)>();
    let mut qi: i64 = b0;
    while qi < tot.len() { let qc: (i64, i64) = tot.get(qi); rd.push((qc.0, qc.1)); qi = qi + 1i64; }

    // |RD| — the quantity the epoch driver will latch into slot 2 as
    // `len(tot) − lat[1]`. There is no driver, so it is computed the same way
    // here and checked against the oracle rather than written into the latch.
    if tot.len() - lat.get(1i64) != rd.len() { return 14i32; }
    if rd.len() != want_rd_n                 { return 15i32; }   // hand-computed

    // RD = closure(PRES) ∖ S, as a set. This is the assertion the ANSWER cannot
    // make: a phase 3 that re-derived the WHOLE closure produces the same final
    // relation and fails only here.
    let mut want_rd: Vec<(i64, i64)> = vec_new::<(i64, i64)>();
    let mut ci: i64 = 0i64;
    while ci < cl_pres.len() {
        let cc: (i64, i64) = cl_pres.get(ci);
        if !pair_has(&s_snap, cc.0, cc.1) { pair_uniq(&mut want_rd, cc.0, cc.1); }
        ci = ci + 1i64;
    }
    if !same_set(&rd, &want_rd) { return 16i32; }

    // RD ⊆ rm — every re-derived row is one PHASE 2 REMOVED. Phase 3 repairs
    // over-deletion and does nothing else; a row in RD that was never in `rm`
    // would mean phase 3 invented a fact rather than restoring one, and the
    // final NET delta a driver folds is `rm ∖ RD` down and nothing up.
    let mut mi: i64 = 0i64;
    while mi < rd.len() {
        let mc: (i64, i64) = rd.get(mi);
        if !pair_has(&rm, mc.0, mc.1) { return 17i32; }
        mi = mi + 1i64;
    }
    // …and the arithmetic that follows from it, stated so the three cardinals
    // cannot drift apart silently: |T| − |rm| + |RD| = |closure(PRES)|.
    if cl_all.len() - rm.len() + rd.len() != cl_pres.len() { return 18i32; }

    // THE SENTINEL, UNCHANGED. `_cpt` returns before phase 3 runs and cannot
    // know |RD|; the round that adds an epoch driver retires this line.
    if lat.get(2i64) != 0i64 - 1i64 { return 19i32; }
    return 0i32;
}

// ── A CHAIN OF `n` EDGES over nodes 1..n+1 — the shape the published timings
// were taken on, and the one shape whose candidate count has a closed form.
fn chain(n: i64) -> Vec<E> {
    let mut v: Vec<E> = vec_new::<E>();
    let mut i: i64 = 1i64;
    while i <= n { v.push(ed(i, i + 1i64)); i = i + 1i64; }
    return v;
}

fn main() -> i32 {
    // ══ CELL 1 — THE CHAIN. `RD = ∅` IS THE ASSERTION. ═══════════════════
    // ALL = 1→2, 2→3, 3→4;  DE = 2→3;  PRES = 1→2, 3→4.
    // T = {12,23,34,13,24,14}                                 — 6
    // OD = {23,24,13,14}                                      — 4
    // S  = {12,34}                                            — 2
    // closure(PRES) = {12,34}                                 — 2
    // RD = closure(PRES) ∖ S = ∅                              — 0
    // Phase 2 alone is already the right answer here, so a phase 3 that
    // re-derives anything at all is caught, and `b0 == |S| == 2` (not 6) is what
    // pins the capture point.
    let mut a1: Vec<E> = vec_new::<E>();
    a1.push(ed(1i64, 2i64)); a1.push(ed(2i64, 3i64)); a1.push(ed(3i64, 4i64));
    let mut d1: Vec<E> = vec_new::<E>();
    d1.push(ed(2i64, 3i64));
    let mut w1: Vec<i64> = vec_new::<i64>();
    let r1: i32 = cell_p3(&a1, &d1, 2i64, 0i64, &mut w1);
    if r1 != 0i32 { return 30i32 + r1; }
    // COST. Round 0 runs the base body over PRES (2 rows) and the recursive
    // body over (S ⋈ PRES) — no `p.b` in S = {(1,2),(3,4)} matches an `e.a`, so
    // the join yields nothing. 2 candidates, ALL DROPPED by the dedup gate,
    // ZERO rows of output.
    if w1.len() != 1i64  { return 21i32; }
    if w1.get(0i64) != 2i64 { return 22i32; }

    // ══ CELL 2 — THE DIAMOND. THE ROUND-0 CELL. ══════════════════════════
    // ALL = 1→2, 1→3, 2→4, 3→4;  DE = 2→4;  PRES = 1→2, 1→3, 3→4.
    // T = {12,13,24,34,14}                                    — 5
    // OD = {24,14}   ((1,4) has a SECOND, surviving derivation and is
    //                 over-deleted anyway — that is the point of DRed)
    // S  = {12,13,34}                                         — 3
    // closure(PRES) = {12,13,34,14}                           — 4
    // RD = {(1,4)}                                            — 1
    // ⚠ (1,4) IS RE-DERIVED FROM TWO OLD FACTS: `path(1,3) ∈ S` joined with
    // `edge(3,4) ∈ PRES`. Neither is a delta of any round, so this row exists in
    // RD ONLY BECAUSE `_i`'s round 0 is a FULL naïve pass over (S × PRES). A
    // round 0 narrowed to the base bodies returns RD = ∅ here and a relation
    // missing a true fact — the measured control at the head of this file.
    let mut a2: Vec<E> = vec_new::<E>();
    a2.push(ed(1i64, 2i64)); a2.push(ed(1i64, 3i64));
    a2.push(ed(2i64, 4i64)); a2.push(ed(3i64, 4i64));
    let mut d2: Vec<E> = vec_new::<E>();
    d2.push(ed(2i64, 4i64));
    let mut w2: Vec<i64> = vec_new::<i64>();
    let r2: i32 = cell_p3(&a2, &d2, 3i64, 1i64, &mut w2);
    if r2 != 0i32 { return 50i32 + r2; }
    // COST. Round 0: base over PRES = 3, plus the join `S(1,3) ⋈ PRES(3,4)` = 1
    // (the one candidate that is genuinely new). Round 1 propagates (1,4) and
    // finds no `e.a == 4`, contributing 0. Total 4 candidates for |RD| = 1 —
    // the only cell in this file where the counter is within 4x of the output.
    if w2.len() != 1i64  { return 23i32; }
    if w2.get(0i64) != 4i64 { return 24i32; }

    // ══ CELL 3 — THE SELF-SUPPORTING CYCLE. PHASE 3 IS THE WHOLE ANSWER. ═
    // ALL = 0→1, 1→2, 2→3, 3→1;  DE = 1→2;  PRES = 0→1, 2→3, 3→1.
    // T = {(0,1),(0,2),(0,3)} ∪ {1,2,3}×{1,2,3}               — 12
    // OD = ALL OF T                                           — 12
    // S  = ∅                                                  — 0
    // closure(PRES) = {(0,1),(2,3),(2,1),(3,1)}               — 4
    // RD = all four                                           — 4
    // Phase 2 leaves NOTHING; the entire correct answer is re-derived. Under any
    // counting/multiplicity scheme the nine pairs among {1,2,3} keep a positive
    // weight forever and nothing is deleted at all — the cell that separates
    // DRed from counting, now with the repair asserted and not just the damage.
    let mut a3: Vec<E> = vec_new::<E>();
    a3.push(ed(0i64, 1i64)); a3.push(ed(1i64, 2i64));
    a3.push(ed(2i64, 3i64)); a3.push(ed(3i64, 1i64));
    let mut d3: Vec<E> = vec_new::<E>();
    d3.push(ed(1i64, 2i64));
    let mut w3: Vec<i64> = vec_new::<i64>();
    let r3: i32 = cell_p3(&a3, &d3, 0i64, 4i64, &mut w3);
    if r3 != 0i32 { return 70i32 + r3; }
    // COST. S = ∅, so round 0's join has nothing on its left and only the base
    // body fires: 3 candidates, all NEW. Round 1 derives (2,1) — 1 candidate.
    // Round 2 finds nothing — 0. Total 4 for |RD| = 4: THE ONLY CELL WHERE THE
    // WORK EQUALS THE OUTPUT, and it is the cell where phase 2 kept nothing,
    // i.e. exactly the case a hybrid would hand to from-scratch anyway.
    if w3.len() != 1i64  { return 25i32; }
    if w3.get(0i64) != 4i64 { return 26i32; }

    // ══ CELL 4 — DE EMPTY. THE PRECISION DIRECTION. ══════════════════════
    // Nothing retracted: OD = ∅, S = T, PRES = ALL, RD = ∅ and the relation must
    // come back UNCHANGED — same rows, same length. Every other cell would pass
    // an `_i` that pushed a second copy of every row it re-derived, because
    // every other cell's S is a strict subset of the closure and the duplicate
    // would hide inside a difference. Here S IS the closure, so a duplicate
    // doubles the length and `same_set` speaks.
    let mut d4: Vec<E> = vec_new::<E>();
    let mut w4: Vec<i64> = vec_new::<i64>();
    let r4: i32 = cell_p3(&a2, &d4, 5i64, 0i64, &mut w4);
    if r4 != 0i32 { return 90i32 + r4; }
    // COST, AND THE CLEAREST SMALL STATEMENT OF THE PESSIMIZATION: NOTHING WAS
    // RETRACTED. |DE| = 0, OD = ∅, S = T, |RD| = 0 — the correct answer is the
    // relation that was already in hand and the correct amount of work is ZERO.
    // `_i` does 6 candidates anyway (4 base + 2 join hits on (1,4)), because
    // round 0 is a full naïve pass and knows nothing about the empty delta.
    if w4.len() != 1i64  { return 27i32; }
    if w4.get(0i64) != 6i64 { return 28i32; }

    // ══ CELL 5 — THE COST GATE. TWO SIZES, SO IT PINS A SHAPE AND NOT A ═══
    // ══ NUMBER. ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    // The published shape: a CHAIN of `n` edges over nodes 1..n+1 with the LAST
    // edge retracted. T = {(i,j) : 1≤i<j≤n+1}, |T| = n(n+1)/2; PRES is the chain
    // of n−1 edges; S = {(i,j) : 1≤i<j≤n}, |S| = n(n−1)/2; and
    //     closure(PRES) = S,  so  RD = ∅  AT EVERY n.
    // A delta pass that did work proportional to its OUTPUT would be FLAT in n
    // here. `_i` is not:
    //
    //   round 0, base body over PRES                        n−1
    //   round 0, recursive body, S ⋈ PRES on p.b == e.a     (n−1)(n−2)/2
    //     — for each (i,j) ∈ S with j ≤ n−1 there is exactly one edge (j,j+1)
    //   ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //   TOTAL                       (n−1) + (n−1)(n−2)/2  =  n(n−1)/2  =  |S|
    //
    // and every one of those candidates is ALREADY IN S, so all are dropped and
    // the fixpoint exits after one round. **THE COUNTER EQUALS |S| EXACTLY AND
    // THE OUTPUT IS EMPTY** — work linear in the relation for zero rows. That
    // identity is what the two sizes assert; a single size would be satisfied by
    // any constant.
    //
    // ⚠ THIS GATE IS PINNING A DEFECT, ON PURPOSE, AND IT MUST GO RED WHEN THE
    // DEFECT IS FIXED. It is the sensor named in `emit_scc_od_fns`'s header for
    // a PESSIMIZATION that no set-oracle in this arc can see and that a
    // wall-clock assertion could only see flakily: measured 2026-08-08 unsharded
    // on an idle box, the whole DRed retraction cost 154 / 971 / 3985 us at
    // |S| = 780 / 3160 / 12720 against from-scratch recompute's
    // 120 / 660 / 2673 — a ratio of 1.28 / 1.47 / 1.49 that GROWS in n. If the
    // ratio deepens because round 0 grew, the numbers below go UP and this cell
    // speaks. When the delta-only round 0 / recompute-hybrid lands, they drop
    // far below |S| and this cell speaks again — and the person landing it
    // restates the identity rather than absorbing it into a suite that stayed
    // green. THAT IS THE POINT: this is the only line in the tree that would
    // notice either direction.
    //
    // ⚠ WHAT IT DOES **NOT** SAY. It is silent about SCAN work: the counter
    // counts candidate ROWS, so a join strategy that scanned more to produce the
    // same tuples reads identically. It is also N = 1 (one SCC member) like
    // every other DRed witness in the tree — see the mutual-recursion gap, open
    // task #16. Both are named here so a reader does not take a green cell for
    // more than it measures.
    let c8: Vec<E> = chain(8i64);
    let mut d8: Vec<E> = vec_new::<E>();
    d8.push(ed(8i64, 9i64));
    let mut w8: Vec<i64> = vec_new::<i64>();
    // |S| = 8·7/2 = 28, |RD| = 0.
    let r8: i32 = cell_p3(&c8, &d8, 28i64, 0i64, &mut w8);
    if r8 != 0i32 { return 150i32 + r8; }
    if w8.len() != 1i64      { return 171i32; }
    if w8.get(0i64) != 28i64 { return 172i32; }   // == |S|, with |RD| = 0

    let c16: Vec<E> = chain(16i64);
    let mut d16: Vec<E> = vec_new::<E>();
    d16.push(ed(16i64, 17i64));
    let mut w16: Vec<i64> = vec_new::<i64>();
    // |S| = 16·15/2 = 120, |RD| = 0. Four times the relation of the n=8 cell.
    let r16: i32 = cell_p3(&c16, &d16, 120i64, 0i64, &mut w16);
    if r16 != 0i32 { return 200i32 + r16; }
    if w16.len() != 1i64       { return 221i32; }
    if w16.get(0i64) != 120i64 { return 222i32; }

    // ⚠ A PROPORTIONALITY CHECK `w16 * 28 == w8 * 120` WAS WRITTEN HERE AND
    // DELETED. With both counts already pinned to literals four lines up it is a
    // branch NO INPUT CAN TAKE — 120·28 == 28·120 is arithmetic, not a
    // measurement — and this tree's rule for exactly that shape is written in
    // `_cpt`'s emitter beside `__keep_<m>`: an equality between two quantities
    // computed the same way from the same rows is not an assertion. What carries
    // the SHAPE here is that there are TWO sizes with INDEPENDENTLY DERIVED
    // numbers (28 and 120, each from n(n−1)/2), not a ratio between them.

    // ══ AND THE ONE THING AN ANSWER ORACLE *WOULD* HAVE CAUGHT, TO SHOW IT
    // ══ WOULD NOT ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    // The diamond again, phase 3 run with `__tot := ∅` — the plan's original
    // phrasing. The final relation is compared against `closure(PRES)` and is
    // CORRECT; only |RD| differs (4 instead of 1). This block asserts the
    // WRONGNESS BY NAME rather than describing it, so that "an answer oracle is
    // blind here" is a measurement this file carries rather than a claim it
    // repeats.
    let p2b: Vec<E> = survivors(&a2, &d2);
    let cl_p2b: Vec<(i64, i64)> = naive_closure(p2b.as_slice());
    let mut z: Vec<(i64, i64)> = vec_new::<(i64, i64)>();
    let mut wz: Vec<i64> = vec_new::<i64>();
    match __wql_tc_scc0_i(p2b.as_slice(), &mut z, &mut wz) {
        Result::Ok(_u) => { } Result::Err(_e) => { return 110i32; }
    }
    if !same_set(&z, &cl_p2b) { return 111i32; }   // THE ANSWER IS RIGHT …
    if z.len() != 4i64        { return 112i32; }   // … and RD would be 4, not 1.
    // ⚠⚠ AND THE COUNTER IS BLIND TO IT TOO — ASSERTED, NOT GLOSSED. The
    // tempting claim is "an answer oracle misses this, so the cost counter
    // catches it". IT DOES NOT. Cell 2 ran this same diamond with `__tot := S`
    // and cost 4 candidates (3 base, all dropped, + the one real join hit).
    // Here, with `__tot := ∅`, round 0's join has an EMPTY left side and does
    // nothing, the 3 base rows are all accepted instead of all dropped, and the
    // join hit arrives one round later: 3 + 1 + 0 = 4 AGAIN. Same count, same
    // answer, different amount of incrementality — the counter senses CANDIDATE
    // ROWS, and this defect moves them between rounds without adding any.
    // What DOES see it is `RD` (4 instead of 1), which is why the |RD| checks
    // stay and the counter is an ADDITION to this file's oracles and not a
    // replacement for one. Pinned by equality so the claim is machine-checked.
    if wz.len() != 1i64             { return 113i32; }
    if wz.get(0i64) != 4i64         { return 114i32; }
    if wz.get(0i64) != w2.get(0i64) { return 115i32; }

    return 0i32;
}
